# Generation speed backlog (hold until Phase 1.5 mobile verify is done)

Pilot feedback (Anthony): Generate Course → preview takes too long. Do **not** implement until the user finishes **Phase 1.5** mobile verify (crop / TOC gutters / Player Properties) and explicitly restarts this work.

## Agreed approach (pilot-safe; prefer same API $)

1. **Parallel hydrate** — bounded concurrency (about 2–3) for `hydrateCourseContent` chunks in [`src/services/aiService.ts`](src/services/aiService.ts); keep retry tiers.
2. **Image pacing** — reduce sequential 1.2–2.0s sleeps and/or pool 2 concurrent calls in [`src/services/imageService.ts`](src/services/imageService.ts).
3. **Perceived speed** — open preview after hydrate (+ cover); continue content images / AI QC async, or defer AI QC past first preview ([`src/App.tsx`](src/App.tsx) `finalizeGeneratedCourse`, [`src/services/qcService.ts`](src/services/qcService.ts)).

## Explicitly deprioritize first

- Throwing money at larger/faster models for every slide (higher cost, unclear wall-clock win).
- Thinning prompts / dropping retries in ways that raise blank-slide risk.

## Context

- Wall clock is dominated by sequential Haiku hydrate + paced images + QC/exam before preview; TTS is already after preview.
- Backend note: full hydrate can be 40–80+ `/api/ai` calls ([`server.js`](server.js)).
